1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:02,110
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:02,170 --> 00:00:03,580
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:05,110
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:07,680
(Episode 20)

5
00:00:40,350 --> 00:00:41,350
I kept you waiting, didn't I?

6
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:43,280
Not at all.

7
00:00:45,020 --> 00:00:47,050
For the new product launch event,

8
00:00:47,120 --> 00:00:49,250
we'll need to free up
some staff beforehand.

9
00:00:49,490 --> 00:00:51,920
Let me know as soon as
you have a date.

10
00:00:53,120 --> 00:00:54,130
Sure.

11
00:00:54,860 --> 00:00:57,760
So, when do you think you'll have
a decision from your team?

12
00:00:59,530 --> 00:01:01,670
I actually just got a call.

13
00:01:01,970 --> 00:01:04,740
It looks like
we'll have to reschedule.

14
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:07,010
Oh, really?

15
00:01:07,970 --> 00:01:09,670
Yes. I'm so sorry.

16
00:01:09,910 --> 00:01:12,540
I'll let you know as soon as
it's been decided.

17
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:14,080
All right. Please do.

18
00:01:16,150 --> 00:01:18,420
By the way,
were you looking for something?

19
00:01:18,720 --> 00:01:19,720
Sorry?

20
00:01:20,450 --> 00:01:23,390
It's just that you kept
looking over at my desk.

21
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:26,620
Oh, your planner.

22
00:01:26,830 --> 00:01:28,760
I saw someone else at the office
with the same one,

23
00:01:28,830 --> 00:01:30,530
and for a second,
I thought it was theirs.

24
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:33,400
This one? I got it from a client.

25
00:01:33,470 --> 00:01:34,470
It's a pretty common design.

26
00:01:34,730 --> 00:01:38,100
I see that now.
Well, I'll be in touch.

27
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:39,570
All right, take care.

28
00:01:44,180 --> 00:01:45,240
(2 p.m., Meeting with
Manager Na Tae Hoon from Cheongma)

29
00:01:45,340 --> 00:01:47,250
(2 p.m., Meeting with
Manager Na Tae Hoon from Cheongma)

30
00:01:47,550 --> 00:01:49,350
(Meeting with Hanbit's
Kim Seong Sik, 2 p.m.)

31
00:01:50,450 --> 00:01:52,150
It's definitely the same person.

32
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:55,120
There's no other way the handwriting
could be this identical.

33
00:01:56,250 --> 00:01:57,260
It seems so.

34
00:01:57,990 --> 00:02:00,260
It looks like he knew
you'd check his schedule...

35
00:02:00,330 --> 00:02:01,760
and made his move in advance.

36
00:02:02,530 --> 00:02:03,530
Then,

37
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:06,100
the one driving the car on June 5...

38
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:07,970
was definitely Manager Na.

39
00:02:08,870 --> 00:02:12,100
Yes, he's our strongest
suspect right now.

40
00:02:14,510 --> 00:02:16,140
But instead of acting rashly,

41
00:02:16,410 --> 00:02:19,240
I think we should find
more solid evidence.

42
00:02:20,180 --> 00:02:22,050
Let's track Manager Na's movements.

43
00:02:22,510 --> 00:02:23,520
Okay.

44
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:26,080
Manager Na
wouldn't have acted alone.

45
00:02:26,580 --> 00:02:28,050
Then I'll try to make contact...

46
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:30,790
by collaborating on tasks
with the PR Team.

47
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:32,560
- Okay.
- Eun Seol.

48
00:02:35,660 --> 00:02:37,800
Let's just hang in there
a little longer.

49
00:02:39,660 --> 00:02:40,670
Okay.

50
00:02:43,740 --> 00:02:45,670
Eun Seol, what's wrong?

51
00:02:47,410 --> 00:02:50,910
I was rushing over here,
and I think I scraped my foot.

52
00:02:51,780 --> 00:02:53,380
Oh, no.

53
00:02:55,750 --> 00:02:56,780
Here, grab it.

54
00:02:57,950 --> 00:02:58,980
I'm okay.

55
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:01,590
I won't be okay with it,
so just grab my arm.

56
00:03:07,730 --> 00:03:08,730
Let's go.

57
00:03:09,390 --> 00:03:12,200
- It's really not that bad.
- Yes, it is.

58
00:03:20,270 --> 00:03:21,610
What's with those two?

59
00:03:21,810 --> 00:03:23,010
I knew they were spending
a lot of time together.

60
00:03:23,070 --> 00:03:24,380
I didn't realize they were an item.

61
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:27,280
Careful.

62
00:03:29,080 --> 00:03:31,180
They aren't even trying
to hide their relationship.

63
00:03:31,250 --> 00:03:32,380
We should be
a little more obvious too.

64
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:35,320
What?

65
00:03:42,530 --> 00:03:43,630
Careful.

66
00:03:52,570 --> 00:03:53,570
There.

67
00:04:10,020 --> 00:04:11,020
Let's go.

68
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:13,760
Careful.

69
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:22,500
Take your time.

70
00:04:22,630 --> 00:04:24,970
(PR Manager, Na Tae Hoon)

71
00:04:28,010 --> 00:04:31,080
- Mr. Kim, what's up?
- Hello, Manager Na.

72
00:04:31,810 --> 00:04:33,110
I trust you're doing well.

73
00:04:33,610 --> 00:04:35,550
Right.
Well, I'm just calling to see...

74
00:04:35,610 --> 00:04:37,880
if a date has been set
for the new product launch event.

75
00:04:39,220 --> 00:04:41,150
The new product launch event?

76
00:04:41,420 --> 00:04:44,690
She used the new product launch
as an excuse to see him?

77
00:04:45,460 --> 00:04:47,890
Yes. This Ko Eun Seol...

78
00:04:48,060 --> 00:04:50,760
seems to be more thorough
than I expected.

79
00:04:51,430 --> 00:04:53,770
Well, that's to be expected.

80
00:04:55,470 --> 00:04:57,900
She couldn't have figured
anything else out, right?

81
00:04:59,670 --> 00:05:01,840
Why are you so nervous, Manager Na?

82
00:05:02,510 --> 00:05:06,240
She's doing exactly what I expected,
which I'm grateful for.

83
00:05:07,880 --> 00:05:09,950
Ko Eun Seol isn't thorough.

84
00:05:10,380 --> 00:05:12,680
She's just scratching the surface
and is pretty naive.

85
00:05:12,980 --> 00:05:14,090
We...

86
00:05:14,420 --> 00:05:16,250
just have to stay one step ahead.

87
00:05:16,790 --> 00:05:19,290
Just one step ahead of Ko Eun Seol.

88
00:05:20,760 --> 00:05:24,200
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

89
00:05:48,790 --> 00:05:49,790
Come in.

90
00:05:51,390 --> 00:05:52,920
What brings you here, Chief Cha?

91
00:05:54,090 --> 00:05:55,130
Please, have a seat.

92
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:57,960
Actually, this isn't something
we should discuss here.

93
00:05:58,800 --> 00:06:00,300
Do you have any plans after work?

94
00:06:01,200 --> 00:06:02,830
No, I don't have
any particular plans.

95
00:06:03,430 --> 00:06:05,040
Then please spare me
some of your time.

96
00:06:06,800 --> 00:06:08,540
It's about Ko Eun Seol.

97
00:06:19,450 --> 00:06:22,320
Eun Seol is a very resilient person.

98
00:06:23,220 --> 00:06:25,220
Given how she was wrongly framed,

99
00:06:25,290 --> 00:06:26,960
it's impressive
that she's held up this well.

100
00:06:32,300 --> 00:06:35,670
What makes you so sure
she was wrongly accused?

101
00:06:37,900 --> 00:06:40,440
It wasn't just because
the witness was bribed.

102
00:06:42,570 --> 00:06:44,610
The desperate look in her eyes...

103
00:06:44,740 --> 00:06:46,380
stayed with me for a long time.

104
00:06:47,810 --> 00:06:49,750
More than any hard evidence,

105
00:06:50,080 --> 00:06:53,380
I was convinced
by that one single look.

106
00:06:56,950 --> 00:06:58,590
What's your relationship
with Eun Seol?

107
00:07:04,630 --> 00:07:07,130
Does what we have
seem that special to you?

108
00:07:14,870 --> 00:07:16,110
I'm curious myself...

109
00:07:16,870 --> 00:07:19,210
about the relationship
between you and Eun Seol.

110
00:07:24,050 --> 00:07:25,520
Based on what she said,

111
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:28,490
I got the impression
there was some awkward history.

112
00:07:30,690 --> 00:07:31,860
Is that what she said?

113
00:07:32,420 --> 00:07:33,960
That we have an awkward history?

114
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:37,730
That's how it seems to me as well.

115
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:44,300
By the way,

116
00:07:46,140 --> 00:07:47,340
do you perhaps...

117
00:07:47,770 --> 00:07:49,810
know anything about Manager Na?

118
00:07:50,370 --> 00:07:51,710
Manager Na from PR?

119
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:54,280
Yes.

120
00:07:56,880 --> 00:07:59,150
There's definitely something
about him.

121
00:08:05,660 --> 00:08:06,660
Never mind.

122
00:08:07,330 --> 00:08:08,590
Would you like another drink?

123
00:08:22,270 --> 00:08:24,540
The desperate look in her eyes...

124
00:08:24,610 --> 00:08:26,680
stayed with me for a long time.

125
00:08:27,680 --> 00:08:29,680
More than any hard evidence,

126
00:08:29,780 --> 00:08:33,120
I was convinced
by that one single look.

127
00:08:37,320 --> 00:08:39,620
Mr. Seok Jin,

128
00:08:39,620 --> 00:08:41,890
I made a mess.

129
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:48,030
I was trying to get you some juice,
but then this happened.

130
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:50,600
It's okay, Mom. I'll clean it up.

131
00:08:58,540 --> 00:09:00,410
Hae Ra, I'll call you back
in a little bit.

132
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:02,150
Are you busy?

133
00:09:02,550 --> 00:09:03,810
Yes, a little.

134
00:09:04,750 --> 00:09:05,780
Oh, right.

135
00:09:05,780 --> 00:09:08,590
You must be swamped
with launching the new brand.

136
00:09:10,660 --> 00:09:12,390
You really have to pull this off.

137
00:09:12,490 --> 00:09:15,090
Our marriage depends
on that shoe brand.

138
00:09:15,660 --> 00:09:19,060
My dad has really high hopes
for this.

139
00:09:19,660 --> 00:09:20,670
Got it?

140
00:09:26,940 --> 00:09:28,210
I'll have to live up
to his expectations.

141
00:09:28,670 --> 00:09:32,180
Okay. I'm trusting you on this.
I love you.

142
00:09:32,580 --> 00:09:33,740
I'll call you back.

143
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:39,020
I'm sorry, Mr. Seok Jin.

144
00:09:39,720 --> 00:09:40,720
It's okay, Mom.

145
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:46,560
That's enough.

146
00:10:07,380 --> 00:10:09,210
Of all people,

147
00:10:09,380 --> 00:10:11,220
I never expected this from you.

148
00:10:12,450 --> 00:10:14,120
To be honest, I'm disappointed.

149
00:10:16,190 --> 00:10:17,820
You don't believe me either?

150
00:10:18,890 --> 00:10:22,530
What are you talking about?
Are you saying you're innocent?

151
00:10:24,430 --> 00:10:26,960
I have absolutely nothing
to be ashamed of.

152
00:10:27,330 --> 00:10:28,470
I'm serious.

153
00:10:28,770 --> 00:10:30,700
Then why was that article published?

154
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:32,740
How would I know?

155
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:35,810
Someone must've targeted me.

156
00:10:36,140 --> 00:10:39,180
Who? Who would target you?

157
00:10:39,940 --> 00:10:41,780
Do you suspect anyone?

158
00:10:41,980 --> 00:10:42,980
No.

159
00:10:43,580 --> 00:10:45,080
No one comes to mind.

160
00:10:45,620 --> 00:10:47,550
That's what's driving me crazy.

161
00:10:56,690 --> 00:10:58,630
So, what's the deal?

162
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:02,070
Is Jong Min having an affair
with that reporter?

163
00:11:02,300 --> 00:11:04,970
No, he says it's fake news.

164
00:11:05,770 --> 00:11:07,100
Fake news?

165
00:11:08,410 --> 00:11:11,040
Someone spread fake news on purpose?

166
00:11:11,340 --> 00:11:13,110
Who? Why on earth?

167
00:11:13,180 --> 00:11:14,250
Who knows?

168
00:11:14,310 --> 00:11:16,880
There are so many strange people
out there these days.

169
00:11:17,480 --> 00:11:20,150
Speaking of which, honey,
go ahead...

170
00:11:20,550 --> 00:11:22,990
with appointing Jong Min
as a board member.

171
00:11:23,690 --> 00:11:25,120
Appoint him as a director?

172
00:11:26,590 --> 00:11:29,130
Why? Is there a problem?

173
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:32,000
Yes.

174
00:11:32,560 --> 00:11:34,170
What's the problem?

175
00:11:34,530 --> 00:11:38,270
I've already chosen someone I know.

176
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:40,540
What? You've chosen someone?

177
00:11:43,510 --> 00:11:47,080
He's Hong Seok Gyu,
a former social welfare professor.

178
00:11:47,140 --> 00:11:50,750
Come on. Just listen to me
and appoint Jong Min.

179
00:11:51,320 --> 00:11:52,320
Unbelievable.

180
00:11:54,350 --> 00:11:57,620
I can't.
I already told Professor Hong.

181
00:11:57,690 --> 00:12:00,760
How can I go back on my word?
I have a reputation to maintain.

182
00:12:01,190 --> 00:12:03,490
Well, if it's too awkward
for you to take it back,

183
00:12:04,030 --> 00:12:05,830
Director Joo can do it.

184
00:12:05,930 --> 00:12:08,800
Director Joo,
you need to take one for the team.

185
00:12:09,170 --> 00:12:10,870
What? Me?

186
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:12,500
I said forget it.

187
00:12:12,740 --> 00:12:16,210
Frankly, Professor Hong is
a much better choice than Jong Min.

188
00:12:16,470 --> 00:12:18,180
It's not just about Professor Hong.

189
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:20,440
His family background
is excellent too.

190
00:12:20,950 --> 00:12:22,780
What? His family?

191
00:12:23,910 --> 00:12:26,280
No, that's not what I meant.

192
00:12:29,120 --> 00:12:30,960
Professor Hong is the right person
for the job,

193
00:12:31,320 --> 00:12:33,820
so just let me have my way
this time.

194
00:12:36,160 --> 00:12:38,460
I'm literally the Chairman
of the scholarship foundation,

195
00:12:38,560 --> 00:12:40,430
so why can't I appoint
a single director the way I want?

196
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:41,630
Fine.

197
00:12:42,100 --> 00:12:45,600
- Do whatever you want.
- Oh my goodness. Honey.

198
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:49,770
What's wrong with him?
Why is he acting like that?

199
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:51,480
Unbelievable.

200
00:12:54,610 --> 00:12:55,850
Maybe I should just...

201
00:12:56,880 --> 00:12:58,550
go with Jong Min.

202
00:12:59,480 --> 00:13:02,520
What are you talking about?
You can't do that, ma'am.

203
00:13:03,020 --> 00:13:05,390
Turns out Jong Min's scandal
is fake news.

204
00:13:06,490 --> 00:13:07,890
And you believe that?

205
00:13:08,160 --> 00:13:10,660
Besides, if you go back on your word
so easily,

206
00:13:10,930 --> 00:13:12,700
what will that do
to your authority as chairman?

207
00:13:12,760 --> 00:13:14,060
We can't have that.

208
00:13:14,130 --> 00:13:15,330
You have a point.

209
00:13:16,570 --> 00:13:19,540
I should use this opportunity
to assert my authority as chairman.

210
00:13:20,500 --> 00:13:22,670
Of course. You should.

211
00:13:32,780 --> 00:13:34,550
Sir, have some honey water.

212
00:13:36,750 --> 00:13:38,890
Was it your recommendation,
Director Joo?

213
00:13:40,090 --> 00:13:42,390
Pardon? What do you mean?

214
00:13:43,930 --> 00:13:47,000
That man, Hong Seok Gyu.
I'm asking if you recommended him.

215
00:13:47,530 --> 00:13:50,500
No, I don't know him at all.

216
00:13:51,540 --> 00:13:52,540
Not at all?

217
00:13:53,840 --> 00:13:54,840
That's right.

218
00:13:57,070 --> 00:13:59,410
All right. You may go.

219
00:14:00,910 --> 00:14:01,910
Right.

220
00:14:21,130 --> 00:14:24,130
Actually, when I was in the US,
I did a bit of research on shoes.

221
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:26,400
My mother suffers
from degenerative arthritis,

222
00:14:26,470 --> 00:14:28,470
so I was wondering
if proper footwear could help her.

223
00:14:28,640 --> 00:14:30,070
Oh, I see.

224
00:14:30,570 --> 00:14:32,040
So instead of just making
simple shoes,

225
00:14:32,110 --> 00:14:34,510
I'm going to focus on them
as functional footwear.

226
00:14:34,980 --> 00:14:37,050
I'll try to implement that
in these new shoes.

227
00:14:37,150 --> 00:14:39,580
But can our team
actually pull this off?

228
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:41,890
Why not?

229
00:14:42,190 --> 00:14:44,050
Our team has designed
and produced the shoes...

230
00:14:44,120 --> 00:14:45,120
for all our fashion shows.

231
00:14:45,190 --> 00:14:46,920
That's right. At last year's show,

232
00:14:46,920 --> 00:14:48,830
the shoes got a better reaction
than the clothes,

233
00:14:48,890 --> 00:14:49,960
which surprised us all.

234
00:14:50,030 --> 00:14:51,660
I'm on board, Chief Cha.

235
00:14:52,800 --> 00:14:54,130
What about you, Ms. Ko?

236
00:14:55,430 --> 00:14:56,430
Pardon?

237
00:14:57,700 --> 00:15:01,070
Oh, right. Yes, I'm on board too.

238
00:15:01,940 --> 00:15:05,040
Ms. Ko, what have you been thinking
so hard about?

239
00:15:06,010 --> 00:15:07,010
Would you rather be elsewhere?

240
00:15:07,680 --> 00:15:09,010
Then sit this one out.

241
00:15:10,180 --> 00:15:12,320
No, that's not it. I'm sorry.

242
00:15:21,960 --> 00:15:22,960
Do you perhaps...

243
00:15:23,730 --> 00:15:25,730
know anything about Manager Na?

244
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:29,000
There's definitely something
about him.

245
00:15:33,370 --> 00:15:34,370
Manager Na.

246
00:15:34,940 --> 00:15:36,770
Chief Cha, hello.

247
00:15:38,640 --> 00:15:40,380
Could I see...

248
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:42,550
the official press release
for our new product?

249
00:15:43,110 --> 00:15:45,020
Of course. Please, come with me.

250
00:15:45,150 --> 00:15:47,120
I was just about to bring it over
for you to review.

251
00:15:52,090 --> 00:15:54,630
(PR Manager, Na Tae Hoon)

252
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:56,090
Just a moment.

253
00:16:06,940 --> 00:16:08,640
I'll go print another copy.

254
00:16:35,230 --> 00:16:38,240
(PR Manager, Na Tae Hoon)

255
00:16:48,080 --> 00:16:49,610
(Ko Eun Seol, out on parole
as a model prisoner)

256
00:16:49,610 --> 00:16:51,380
(As expected, Seo Hyun Jae
stops by General Affairs.)

257
00:16:56,150 --> 00:16:57,590
(Ko Eun Seol,
list of department managers?)

258
00:16:57,590 --> 00:16:59,020
(Double-check schedule.)

259
00:17:06,200 --> 00:17:07,430
Here it is.

260
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,470
Once the revisions are ready,
I'll report to you immediately.

261
00:17:11,540 --> 00:17:12,700
Yes, thank you.

262
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:14,540
Thank you for your help.

263
00:17:23,350 --> 00:17:24,480
What's this?

264
00:17:25,550 --> 00:17:26,920
It's Manager Na's notepad.

265
00:17:28,620 --> 00:17:32,090
I don't know what you
and Ms. Ko are looking for,

266
00:17:32,560 --> 00:17:34,790
but this didn't seem
entirely unrelated.

267
00:17:36,130 --> 00:17:37,800
Check out what's inside it.

268
00:17:39,800 --> 00:17:40,900
Chief Cha.

269
00:17:44,270 --> 00:17:47,910
Tell Ms. Ko you just happened
to stumble across this.

270
00:18:00,320 --> 00:18:03,450
- What could be delicious?
- What could be good?

271
00:18:04,560 --> 00:18:05,920
Mister!

272
00:18:07,890 --> 00:18:09,060
Are you insane?

273
00:18:09,460 --> 00:18:12,360
What are you doing half-naked
in the middle of the day?

274
00:18:12,430 --> 00:18:13,730
My gosh. Don't look.

275
00:18:14,200 --> 00:18:15,200
You're back.

276
00:18:15,530 --> 00:18:18,100
I'm just letting my muscles
soak up some sun for a change.

277
00:18:18,740 --> 00:18:19,800
You're familiar with tanning, right?

278
00:18:20,940 --> 00:18:23,570
You don't get a body like this
for free, you know.

279
00:18:23,570 --> 00:18:25,040
Get up already.

280
00:18:25,810 --> 00:18:28,410
That darker skin makes me think
of pig's feet. Unbelievable.

281
00:18:29,410 --> 00:18:31,850
Pig's feet? Come on.

282
00:18:33,250 --> 00:18:35,290
Have you ever seen trotters
this sexy?

283
00:18:36,120 --> 00:18:37,120
Pig's feet?

284
00:18:37,550 --> 00:18:41,060
Calling the only son
of three generations pig's feet?

285
00:18:41,260 --> 00:18:44,160
Ma'am, you need to get
your grandson under control.

286
00:18:44,230 --> 00:18:45,660
It's the middle of the day!

287
00:18:46,660 --> 00:18:48,600
This is incredibly rude
to your neighbors.

288
00:18:48,670 --> 00:18:51,800
There she goes again,
pulling the landlord card.

289
00:18:51,970 --> 00:18:54,100
Just because she owns
this one tiny house,

290
00:18:54,100 --> 00:18:56,370
she lords it over us.

291
00:18:56,570 --> 00:18:57,840
Ma'am!

292
00:18:58,310 --> 00:18:59,540
You, get dressed.

293
00:19:00,140 --> 00:19:02,110
You're precious enough
fully clothed,

294
00:19:02,180 --> 00:19:04,410
so why are you half-naked like this?

295
00:19:04,720 --> 00:19:05,920
This woman...

296
00:19:06,380 --> 00:19:08,520
was already checking you out.

297
00:19:08,590 --> 00:19:09,950
When did I ever do that?

298
00:19:10,820 --> 00:19:11,990
- Mom.
- Yes?

299
00:19:11,990 --> 00:19:14,760
Mom, I want to be
a sexy pig's trotter too.

300
00:19:15,130 --> 00:19:16,130
What?

301
00:19:16,860 --> 00:19:18,000
You want to be one too?

302
00:19:23,270 --> 00:19:24,270
Here.

303
00:19:26,500 --> 00:19:28,470
But for you, Teun Teun,
sexy is a bit much.

304
00:19:29,170 --> 00:19:30,470
How about a tough one instead?

305
00:19:30,470 --> 00:19:33,380
Sounds good.
I'm a tough pig's trotter.

306
00:19:33,840 --> 00:19:35,980
Seo Teun Teun, get down from there.
Come here.

307
00:19:36,180 --> 00:19:38,020
I told you to put your clothes on.

308
00:19:39,350 --> 00:19:43,450
Lee Jung Tae going to Vietnam,
and his mother moving away,

309
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:45,390
I think Manager Na
was behind it all.

310
00:19:45,960 --> 00:19:48,190
He knew that I had
the list of directors,

311
00:19:49,160 --> 00:19:51,560
and that I'd checked
their schedules.

312
00:19:51,630 --> 00:19:54,400
It seems he's anticipating
your every move.

313
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:56,000
Will you be okay?

314
00:19:57,300 --> 00:19:59,600
Instead of a surprise attack
to catch them off guard,

315
00:20:00,070 --> 00:20:02,710
how about we slowly
tighten the screws?

316
00:20:02,870 --> 00:20:06,440
We might have missed something,
so we should be careful.

317
00:20:09,380 --> 00:20:11,780
We're really almost at the end.

318
00:20:13,350 --> 00:20:16,190
By the way,
where did you get this notepad?

319
00:20:17,250 --> 00:20:19,960
Oh, I found it.
By chance, in the hallway.

320
00:20:20,620 --> 00:20:21,790
Really?

321
00:20:22,430 --> 00:20:24,330
What a relief.

322
00:20:26,960 --> 00:20:27,970
Eun Seol.

323
00:20:29,100 --> 00:20:31,840
This isn't something
you can just laugh off.

324
00:20:32,600 --> 00:20:34,200
It could be really dangerous.

325
00:20:35,510 --> 00:20:36,510
I know.

326
00:20:37,040 --> 00:20:39,810
But it seems like
you're enjoying it somehow.

327
00:20:42,410 --> 00:20:44,150
For the first time in ten years,

328
00:20:44,210 --> 00:20:46,120
they're going to be scared
because of me.

329
00:20:47,250 --> 00:20:50,750
Can't I enjoy that just a bit?

330
00:20:54,490 --> 00:20:57,390
Don't worry. I won't cross the line.

331
00:20:58,060 --> 00:21:00,400
You have to remember you said that.

332
00:21:01,060 --> 00:21:02,070
I will.

333
00:21:06,300 --> 00:21:08,310
Looks like you haven't
had dinner yet, have you?

334
00:21:08,740 --> 00:21:10,840
I haven't, and I'm starving.

335
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:12,940
Should I buy you dinner?

336
00:21:13,310 --> 00:21:14,810
No, it's okay. I'll eat at home.

337
00:21:15,910 --> 00:21:17,250
All right.
You should head home, then.

338
00:21:17,810 --> 00:21:18,820
Okay.

339
00:21:27,760 --> 00:21:29,460
Did you find anything else out?

340
00:21:32,030 --> 00:21:33,360
It's not certain,

341
00:21:33,430 --> 00:21:35,670
but I think I'm starting to identify
the people around the real killer.

342
00:21:36,030 --> 00:21:37,530
What? Really?

343
00:21:37,930 --> 00:21:39,970
Is there anything else
I can do to help?

344
00:21:40,740 --> 00:21:43,210
Last time I was a detective,
so this time...

345
00:21:43,440 --> 00:21:45,380
I could play a guard
or maybe a delivery driver.

346
00:21:45,810 --> 00:21:49,180
Should I try to sneak in
disguised as one of them?

347
00:21:51,080 --> 00:21:52,080
Dad,

348
00:21:52,920 --> 00:21:54,790
thank you so much
for believing in me...

349
00:21:54,850 --> 00:21:55,990
and being on my side.

350
00:21:57,150 --> 00:22:01,630
If a time comes when I need help,
I'll let you know.

351
00:22:02,090 --> 00:22:03,690
Just say the word.

352
00:22:04,060 --> 00:22:06,260
I'd do anything for my daughter.

353
00:22:08,230 --> 00:22:09,230
Eun Seol.

354
00:22:10,100 --> 00:22:11,100
You trust your dad, right?

355
00:22:12,500 --> 00:22:14,270
Yes, I do.

356
00:22:28,920 --> 00:22:31,960
(2S6 2751)

357
00:22:32,020 --> 00:22:35,230
It wasn't me. Hey!

358
00:22:35,690 --> 00:22:37,390
Let me go!

359
00:22:39,300 --> 00:22:40,530
Hey!

360
00:23:10,730 --> 00:23:11,760
Manager Na.

361
00:23:18,800 --> 00:23:21,910
Oh, hey.
Ms. Ko, what brings you here?

362
00:23:23,740 --> 00:23:24,740
This.

363
00:23:26,580 --> 00:23:27,780
I think this is yours, Manager Na.

364
00:23:29,910 --> 00:23:32,350
Oh, right. Thank you.

365
00:23:34,620 --> 00:23:35,850
I found it in the hallway.

366
00:23:37,820 --> 00:23:39,620
But in this notepad
I stumbled across,

367
00:23:40,590 --> 00:23:42,890
I noticed quite a few
familiar names.

368
00:23:43,890 --> 00:23:47,260
What? Familiar names?

369
00:23:47,900 --> 00:23:50,200
From people I know well...

370
00:23:51,640 --> 00:23:53,700
to people I've been
desperately searching for.

371
00:23:55,640 --> 00:23:58,910
I have no idea what that means.

372
00:24:00,810 --> 00:24:01,810
Exactly.

373
00:24:03,450 --> 00:24:04,820
As for what this is all about,

374
00:24:05,950 --> 00:24:07,950
I intend to find out,
little by little.

375
00:24:11,660 --> 00:24:12,660
Well then.

376
00:24:41,280 --> 00:24:42,290
Are you okay?

377
00:24:43,290 --> 00:24:44,490
You don't look well.

378
00:24:46,460 --> 00:24:48,990
I'm fine. I'm just a little tired.

379
00:24:54,060 --> 00:24:55,900
Don't just charge ahead.

380
00:24:58,170 --> 00:24:59,940
Sometimes you need to take
the long way around.

381
00:25:01,710 --> 00:25:02,840
And most importantly...

382
00:25:05,340 --> 00:25:06,640
Take care of yourself first.

383
00:25:09,150 --> 00:25:11,080
You look exhausted,
in body and mind.

384
00:25:18,320 --> 00:25:19,620
I'm doing fine.

385
00:25:21,260 --> 00:25:23,790
And I'm not as exhausted
as you think.

386
00:25:25,330 --> 00:25:26,530
This is just the beginning.

387
00:25:28,330 --> 00:25:29,430
As for the past,

388
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:32,270
I'm going to uncover it all
on my own.

389
00:25:35,740 --> 00:25:36,740
Relax a little.

390
00:25:40,080 --> 00:25:42,280
You don't have to pretend
you're okay with me.

391
00:25:47,850 --> 00:25:48,850
Seok Jin.

392
00:25:50,990 --> 00:25:51,990
Hey.

393
00:25:52,960 --> 00:25:54,420
Why are you two together?

394
00:25:55,990 --> 00:25:57,130
We just ran into each other.

395
00:25:58,190 --> 00:25:59,700
Well, that feels unsettling.

396
00:26:01,930 --> 00:26:04,230
Go up to the office
and print out the design drafts.

397
00:26:05,700 --> 00:26:06,700
Sure.

398
00:26:07,870 --> 00:26:09,240
Let's go get some coffee.

399
00:26:09,810 --> 00:26:10,810
Okay.

400
00:26:24,850 --> 00:26:27,260
So you're saying Ko Eun Seol
brought this to you?

401
00:26:28,020 --> 00:26:29,030
Yes.

402
00:26:30,430 --> 00:26:32,000
I don't know
how I could've dropped it.

403
00:26:32,630 --> 00:26:34,730
I'm always so careful.

404
00:26:35,130 --> 00:26:36,870
Manager Na,
do you actually believe her?

405
00:26:38,300 --> 00:26:39,340
What?

406
00:26:39,340 --> 00:26:40,970
She went through
the managers' offices...

407
00:26:41,140 --> 00:26:43,040
to check their schedules.

408
00:26:43,540 --> 00:26:45,380
She must've stolen this.

409
00:26:45,580 --> 00:26:47,210
Do you really think
she just found it?

410
00:26:48,710 --> 00:26:51,820
Then Ko Eun Seol was intentionally
after this notepad?

411
00:26:54,050 --> 00:26:57,150
Are you that dense?
What exactly have you been doing?

412
00:26:59,020 --> 00:27:00,190
I'm sorry, Ms. Joo.

413
00:27:02,130 --> 00:27:03,430
So what do we do now?

414
00:27:03,430 --> 00:27:05,130
If she saw this notepad,

415
00:27:05,200 --> 00:27:07,900
she'd know
that I contacted Lee Jung Tae.

416
00:27:08,970 --> 00:27:11,330
The breadcrumbs will lead
back to you, and...

417
00:27:11,330 --> 00:27:13,170
That's why the notepad...

418
00:27:16,570 --> 00:27:18,070
Try not to make it obvious...

419
00:27:19,580 --> 00:27:21,140
and act like everything is normal.

420
00:27:21,980 --> 00:27:23,210
From now on,

421
00:27:23,210 --> 00:27:24,980
Ko Eun Seol will have her eye
on you.

422
00:27:27,480 --> 00:27:28,720
It's only a matter of time...

423
00:27:28,790 --> 00:27:30,550
before she finds out
I'm behind this.

424
00:27:31,720 --> 00:27:32,720
Right.

425
00:27:33,160 --> 00:27:35,960
You have to weed out
the bad ones early on.

426
00:27:42,670 --> 00:27:43,670
Tae Hoon.

427
00:27:51,570 --> 00:27:52,940
To clear our heads,

428
00:27:53,810 --> 00:27:55,280
shall we go visit that place?

429
00:28:25,380 --> 00:28:27,740
This place hasn't changed at all.

430
00:28:29,750 --> 00:28:31,010
We're the only ones who've changed.

431
00:28:32,980 --> 00:28:34,050
Still,

432
00:28:34,150 --> 00:28:38,620
they built a resort
where the orphanage used to be.

433
00:28:40,760 --> 00:28:43,490
The view from there
was incredible back then.

434
00:28:45,300 --> 00:28:46,300
It was.

435
00:28:47,100 --> 00:28:49,000
I used to stare
at that river every day...

436
00:28:49,530 --> 00:28:53,140
and vow to myself
that I would escape one day.

437
00:28:54,370 --> 00:28:56,310
I was so sick of that river.

438
00:28:59,410 --> 00:29:00,410
Ae Sook.

439
00:29:03,180 --> 00:29:05,480
It's okay to call you that here,
right?

440
00:29:06,820 --> 00:29:09,350
Here, we aren't Manager Na
and Director Joo.

441
00:29:10,890 --> 00:29:14,620
You're Ae Sook, who looked after me
back at the orphanage.

442
00:29:16,390 --> 00:29:19,000
Coming here made me want
to call you that.

443
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:25,000
Sure.

444
00:29:26,640 --> 00:29:28,540
Let's forget everything,
just for today.

445
00:29:29,270 --> 00:29:30,770
Work and even Ko Eun Seol.

446
00:29:31,110 --> 00:29:33,340
Let's forget it all
and be our old selves.

447
00:29:34,910 --> 00:29:35,910
Sure.

448
00:29:36,410 --> 00:29:39,050
Ae Sook, want to go for a drive...

449
00:29:39,420 --> 00:29:42,090
and check out the resort built
on the former orphanage grounds?

450
00:29:43,050 --> 00:29:44,050
Sounds good.

451
00:30:32,270 --> 00:30:33,400
It's so sweet.

452
00:30:35,740 --> 00:30:37,940
I wanted this so badly
when we were kids.

453
00:30:40,140 --> 00:30:42,380
Tae Hoon, do you remember?

454
00:30:44,280 --> 00:30:45,280
You and I...

455
00:30:45,920 --> 00:30:48,120
wanted this banana milk so badly...

456
00:30:49,250 --> 00:30:51,890
that we stole some
and got caught by the director.

457
00:30:54,520 --> 00:30:57,630
Even as we were
getting beaten back then,

458
00:30:58,630 --> 00:31:00,560
we cried our eyes out...

459
00:31:00,830 --> 00:31:02,400
just because we couldn't drink
that banana milk.

460
00:31:06,470 --> 00:31:09,210
At least you had your fill
before the end came.

461
00:31:09,840 --> 00:31:10,840
Right?

462
00:31:12,780 --> 00:31:14,210
Now, forget everything
that happened here.

463
00:31:14,880 --> 00:31:16,210
Go on ahead and rest in peace.

464
00:31:18,480 --> 00:31:20,850
(To Ko Eun Seol)

465
00:32:03,260 --> 00:32:04,290
Seriously?

466
00:32:37,690 --> 00:32:41,530
(A Trap Called Desire)

467
00:32:41,600 --> 00:32:43,200
They're saying Manager Na is dead!

468
00:32:43,200 --> 00:32:44,770
Detective, what kind of nonsense...

469
00:32:45,600 --> 00:32:47,670
The one who actually
killed my mom...

470
00:32:49,640 --> 00:32:51,510
I'll take moral responsibility
for Manager Na's death...

471
00:32:51,510 --> 00:32:52,780
and step down, ma'am.

472
00:32:53,010 --> 00:32:54,940
Don't you know we can't do
without you, Director Joo?

473
00:32:54,940 --> 00:32:57,780
Has Director Joo ever told us
about her family?

474
00:32:57,950 --> 00:32:59,650
As the head of this family,

475
00:32:59,650 --> 00:33:01,150
I've gathered you all
to say something.

476
00:33:01,320 --> 00:33:03,250
You're saying someone else
was behind the murder?

477
00:33:03,250 --> 00:33:04,750
Looks like
you've achieved your goal,

478
00:33:04,820 --> 00:33:05,860
so how about you get lost?

479
00:33:06,090 --> 00:33:09,190
Now, Ko Eun Seol, what will you do?

480
00:33:09,260 --> 00:33:10,430
Is this pride talking?

481
00:33:10,490 --> 00:33:13,100
You insolent little girl
who doesn't know her place.

482
00:33:13,800 --> 00:33:15,770
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
